From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:18:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: macsmc: Keep the suspend-to-idle SMC handshake
 opt-in

The sleep handshake (WKTP = 2, MBSE = 'slpa'/'waka') was made on by
default for every system sleep. Suspend-to-RAM needs it, but under
suspend-to-idle it changes nothing measurable (the commit that added it
says so) and it is new SMC traffic on the path every installed J604
kernel uses today.

Make suspend-to-idle behave exactly as before unless sleep_handshake=1
is given, and always make the handshake for suspend-to-RAM, which is
itself only offered with apple_s2r.enable=1.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/mfd/macsmc.c | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/macsmc.c b/drivers/mfd/macsmc.c
index 39fb1c7073..7a79fa8aea 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/macsmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/macsmc.c
@@ -642,17 +642,19 @@ static int apple_smc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
  * bitmap and announce the wake with MBSE = 'waka', which clears that bit.
  *
  * The announcement only tells the SMC that the system is asleep; it does not
- * by itself power anything down under s2idle. It can be disabled with the
- * sleep_handshake module parameter. MBSW is read-only and always logged.
+ * by itself power anything down under s2idle. Under s2idle it is only made
+ * with the sleep_handshake module parameter (default off, so suspend-to-idle
+ * behaves as before); suspend-to-RAM, which needs it, always makes it. MBSW
+ * is read-only and always logged.
  *
  * For suspend-to-RAM, defer the announcement to suspend_late and then notify
  * RTKit that the AP is asleep, leaving the SMC itself running. Block key
  * commands until resume_early acknowledges the AP wake, including on abort.
  * The RTKit acknowledgment needs interrupts and its non-freezable worker.
  */
-static bool sleep_handshake = true;
+static bool sleep_handshake;
 module_param(sleep_handshake, bool, 0644);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(sleep_handshake, "Announce system sleep and wake to the SMC (default: on)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(sleep_handshake, "Also announce suspend-to-idle and its wake to the SMC; suspend-to-RAM always does (default: off)");
 
 static int apple_smc_announce_sleep(struct device *dev)
 {
@@ -660,7 +662,7 @@ static int apple_smc_announce_sleep(struct device *dev)
 	int ret;
 
 	smc->sleep_announced = false;
-	if (!sleep_handshake)
+	if (!sleep_handshake && pm_suspend_target_state != PM_SUSPEND_MEM)
 		return 0;
 
 	if (apple_smc_key_exists(smc, SMC_KEY(WKTP))) {
